  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A block of ice of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is put in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of water at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of ice melts as the temperature of the water reaches <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is</p><p>[Use: Specific heat capacity of water <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>kg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, Latent heat of ice <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>kg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "90",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>According to the principle of calorimetry, heat lost by hot body is equal to the heat gained by cold body.</p><p>The heat&nbsp;released by water</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4200</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>31500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p>let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> ice melts then,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>31500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>31500</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9000</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>09</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
